# renode-test run artifacts (renode/README.md "Running it"): regenerated on
# every `renode-test renode/ws500.robot` invocation, so they don't belong in
# version control. This file is scoped to renode/ deliberately -- the
# repo-root .gitignore covers unrelated build/tooling output and is owned
# separately.
log.html
report.html
robot_output.xml
# --save-logs (default: onfail) and the Robot "Create Snapshot Of Failed
# Test" hook write here whenever a case fails locally; same reasoning.
logs/
snapshots/
# renode-test also writes results-<suite>.robot.xml next to the suite when
# invoked with -r; same category as the artifacts above.
results-*.xml
